(Chapter 4 - Linear Equations) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 740 Tm
(4.1  Introduction) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 720 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 60 700 Tm
(An equation is a statement that two expressions are equal.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 680 Tm
(A linear equation in one variable has the general form:) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 660 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 60 640 Tm
(        ax + b = 0        where a is not equal to 0) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 620 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 60 600 Tm
(The value of x that satisfies the equation is called its) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 580 Tm
(solution or root.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 560 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 60 540 Tm
(Example 1:  Solve  3x + 5 = 20) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 520 Tm
(            3x = 20 - 5) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 500 Tm
(            3x = 15) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 480 Tm
(             x = 5) Tj
